description:
**Location**: flush.rs:227-240

**Issue**: Flush loads entire memtable into a Vec, then sorts. For 256MB memtable = 512MB+ peak memory allocation.

```rust
let mut all_entries: Vec<(InternalKey, Bytes)> = Vec::new();
for partition_mt in &flushing_partitions {
    for (ikey, value) in partition_mt.iter() {
        all_entries.push((ikey, value));
    }
}
all_entries.sort_by(|(k1, _), (k2, _)| k1.cmp(k2));
```

**Impact**: OOM on memory-constrained systems during flush.

**Fix**: Use k-way merge streaming (partitions are already sorted) instead of collect-sort.
